# D51 / `todo/t0718` — `unify`'s smart-pointer coercion is keyed on the TYPED
# builtin IDENTITY (`DefInfo.builtin_kind`), never on the definition's NAME.
#
# ⛔ D51, VERBATIM, ON THE ONE-WORD EDIT THIS ROW EXISTS TO STOP: adding `Box`
# to the coercion list *"would make the symptom go away while preserving the
# defect, and is not an acceptable fix."*
#
# `Box[Concrete]` → `Box[Trait]` (D51's own subject, `todo/t0710`) is a TRAIT
# OBJECT upcast and wants a real `TraitObject` arm in `unify`. Making `Box`
# coercion-transparent instead would make `Box[int]` unify with `int` — this
# program — and with everything else its inner unifies with.
#
# ⚠ THE ACCESSOR-PARITY UNIT TESTS CANNOT REPLACE THIS ROW AND THIS ROW CANNOT
# REPLACE THEM. Adding `Box` to the accessor is invisible to a seed-coverage
# test (every `DefId` still carries the right identity); deleting a seed site is
# invisible to a pure-function parity test. Both guards ship, and this row is
# the fixture-level half — measured: it flips rc 1 → 0 under that one edit.
# Asserted by `coercion_identity_box_is_not_coercion_transparent`.

int take_int(int x):
    return x + 1

void show(Box[int] b):
    print(take_int(b))

void main():
    show(Box(5))
